# Huawei VRP display interface transceiver parser.
#
# Sample input (templates/samples/huawei_10_62_25_253_display_interface_transceiver.txt):
#   10GE5/0/4 transceiver information:
#   -------------------------------------------------------------------
#    Common information:
#      Transceiver Type                      :1000BASE_SX
#      ...
#    Manufacture information:
#      Manu. Serial Number                   :8000012000082
#      Manufacturing Date                    :2025-2-20
#
# Field semantics:
#   INTERFACE — device interface name (e.g. 10GE5/0/4).
#   SN        — vendor manufacturing serial number (Manu. Serial Number).
#
# Strategy: every block starts with `<INTERFACE> transceiver information:`.
# The parser captures INTERFACE without recording, then matches the
# Manu. Serial Number line later and triggers Record there. Variables
# without Filldown keyword persist across lines within the in-progress
# record because the parser does not reset CurrentRecord between matches.
#
# The homegrown textfsm parser (internal/templates/textfsm.go) only
# recognises the `-> Record` / `-> Continue` / `-> Error` / `-> State`
# transitions; the `Continue.Record` style used by some templates is a
# no-op and is intentionally not used here.
#
# D-10 (RESEARCH Pitfall 5): the Wave 2 collector filters transceiver
# rows by the up-interface list produced by display interface status
# BEFORE parsing this template. The template itself just extracts every
# transceiver block; the Go collector applies the up-filter post-parse.

Value INTERFACE (\S+)
Value SN (\S+)

Start
  ^\s*${INTERFACE}\s+transceiver\s+information:\s*$$
  ^\s*Manu\.\s+Serial\s+Number\s*:\s*${SN}\s*$$ -> Record
